{"symbol":"FRES.L","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-09T20:09:21Z","info":{"address1":"Calzada Legaria No. 549","address2":"Torre 2, Piso 11 Colonia 10 de abril DelegaciOn Miguel Hidalgo","city":"Mexico City","state":"DF","zip":"11250","country":"Mexico","phone":"52 55 5279 3000","website":"https://www.fresnilloplc.com","industry":"Other Precious Metals & Mining","industryKey":"other-precious-metals-mining","industryDisp":"Other Precious Metals & Mining","sector":"Basic Materials","sectorKey":"basic-materials","sectorDisp":"Basic Materials","longBusinessSummary":"Fresnillo plc mines, develops, and produces non-ferrous minerals in Mexico. It operates through seven segments: Fresnillo, Saucito, Ciénega, Herradura, Noche Buena, San Julián, and Juanicipio. The company primarily explores for silver, gold, lead, and zinc concentrates. Its projects include the Fresnillo silver mine located in the state of Zacatecas; Saucito mine situated in the state of Zacatecas; Ciénega mine located in the state of Durango; Herradura mine located in the state of Sonora; Noche Buena mine located in the state of Sonora; San Julián mine situated on the border of Chihuahua/Durango states; and Juanicipio mine located in the state of Zacatecas. The company also leases mining equipment; produces lead, silver and zinc concentrates and silver precipitates; produces gold/silver doré bars; mines projects; and provides exploration and administrative services. Fresnillo plc was founded in 1887 and is headquartered in Mexico City, Mexico. Fresnillo plc is a subsidiary of Industrias Peñoles, S.A.B. de C.V.","fullTimeEmployees":7348,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Octavio M. Alvidrez","age":60,"title":"Chief Executive Officer","yearBorn":1965,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1537233,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Mario  Arreguin","age":68,"title":"Chief Financial Officer","yearBorn":1957,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"nam